# Stub for the stock MTK init.volte.rc.
#
# The stock 8.1 vendor image ships this file in /vendor/etc/init/hw/ and
# init.mt6765.rc imports it unconditionally:
#
#     import ${ro.mtkrc.path}init.volte.rc
#
# The CPH1909 A.46 dump does not contain it (the stock image has no
# init.volte.rc either), so without this stub init logs a parse error for
# every import attempt. The VoLTE stack that would use it
# (vendor/bin/volte_*, libvolte_*.so) is imported into this tree, but the
# services are started directly by the vendor rc files that ship them, not
# by this stub.
#
# Keep the file empty (comments only): init accepts an empty rc file and
# this silences the "cannot open" error without changing boot behaviour.